---
description: "House writing style for this repo"
globs: ["**/*.md", "**/*.mdx", "**/*.txt", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.py"]
---

You are editing an existing, real production codebase.

Always follow this style:

- Tone: concise, professional, founder/engineer voice. No marketing fluff, no generic AI blog style.
- Never use emojis or emoticons.
- Never write phrases like "as an AI", "language model", "I cannot", "I am just an AI", or anything that reveals AI authorship.
- Prefer short, direct sentences over long, chatty explanations.
- Be specific and technical when explaining behavior, avoid vague motivational language.

When editing:
- Do NOT change code behavior.
- Do NOT invent new features or APIs.
- For Markdown and docs: keep headings, code blocks, and lists; just rewrite the surrounding prose.
- For comments: keep intent and meaning, but rewrite the text to match the style above.

If a section already matches this style, leave it unchanged.
